([CASE STUDY 4: Engineering Ethics: Lessons from Catastrophic Failures]) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
/F2 9.5 Tf
(-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Context: Examine historic engineering catastrophes caused by ethical compromises and) Tj
T*
(software/hardware defects.) Tj
T*
(Ethical Case Analysis:) Tj
T*
(* 1. Therac-25 Radiation Overdose Disaster \(1985-1987\): Radiation therapy machine) Tj
T*
(delivered lethal overdoses to cancer patients. Root Cause: Software race condition) Tj
T*
(and elimination of physical hardware interlocks that previously prevented) Tj
T*
(simultaneous high-power beam operation. Ethical Lesson: Safety-critical systems must) Tj
T*
(NEVER rely solely on software; independent hardware fail-safe interlocks are) Tj
T*
(mandatory.) Tj
T*
(* 2. Volkswagen Emissions "Defeat Device" Scandal \(2015\): Software algorithms) Tj
T*
(detected when vehicle was undergoing laboratory emissions testing and activated full) Tj
T*
(emission controls, while deactivating them during real-world driving. Ethical Lesson:) Tj
T*
(Engineering deception destroys company credibility, violates environmental laws, and) Tj
T*
(directly breaches IEEE Code of Ethics.) Tj
T*
(* 3. Professional Commitment: The ethical engineer holds human safety, product) Tj
T*
(transparency, and data integrity above commercial expedience.) Tj
T*
